to resolve the issue in the long term.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The TMJ specialists featured in this list all have an extensive range of medical accreditations and qualifications across premier institutions in India and beyond. However, before getting into the list of specialists, let\u2019s take a closer look at the nuances a TMJ specialist can provide over a general dentist.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Choose a TMJ Specialist in India?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Accurate Identification: <\/strong>Some of TMD\u2019s symptoms closely resemble that of other orofacial conditions such as sinusitis. A TMJ specialist can help pinpoint the incidence of TMJ dysfunction with accurate diagnosis.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Effective Treatment: <\/strong>Proper treatment of TMD requires a holistic approach that takes into consideration various factors such as the severity of symptoms and disorder progression. A TMJ specialist will provide 360-degree treatment for long-term recovery from TMD.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Attention to pain factor and comfort: <\/strong>In some minor cases, a TMJ specialist in India will recommend targeted physiotherapy to alleviate the symptoms of TMD, placing your comfort foremost for hassle-free treatment.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The above attributes hint at the innate complexity of TMJ conditions, and the care required to treat them in the long run. To that end, let\u2019s shed some light on the intricacies of the TMJ, the risk factors for TMD, and telltale signs of TMJ dysfunction.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">TMJ In Focus: Risk Factors &amp; Symptoms<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ issues revolve around the temporomandibular joint as well as the muscles and ligaments that surround it. Therefore, TMJ disorders are considered a spectrum, with multiple possible causes. Currently, there are over 30 conditions that are known to affect the TMJ region.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If left unchecked, TMJ disorders can lead to long-term chronic conditions that typically worsen over time. Some of these include:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Grinding of teeth<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Jaw trauma<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tenderness in the temporomandibular joint<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ issues can be further categorised into the specific part of the framework that causes issues. For instance, the TMD could be caused by a <strong>displaced disc <\/strong>or a <strong>strained muscle. <\/strong>The best TMJ specialists in India are well-equipped to treat these conditions, with thorough diagnosis and focused treatment plans.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To better understand what TMJ disorders can look like at the onset, here is a quick reference list of risk factors that the top 10 TMJ specialists in India typically advise patients on:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Risk factors:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Stress<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Severe trauma in the jaw<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Genetics<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Lower pain tolerance<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stress in facial muscles<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Habits (frequent clenching of the jaw)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>What does TMD look like?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Clicking\/popping in the jaw region<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pain during chewing\/speaking<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chronic ear pain<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pain in the area around your eyes<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>A feeling of tightness in the head\/temples<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Jaw locking at the joint region<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is important to note that in most TMD cases, not all these symptoms may occur in a single instance. In a broad sense, the two general symptoms of TMJ disorders are <strong>joint locking (with ensuing sounds), <\/strong>and <strong>jaw pain <\/strong>of varying degrees.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Treatment <\/strong>for TMJ conditions typically depends on the causative factors and the specific site of the issue. Your TMJ specialist in India will prescribe treatment based on comprehensive factors such as your medical history and response to previous dental treatments. Some of the specific treatment methods for TMJ disorders are:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8211; <strong>Physiotherapy:<\/strong> Minor cases of TMJ disorders often subside after dedicated physiotherapy treatment in the affected region. This is especially true in cases where muscle strain is the root cause.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8211; <strong>Disc displacement treatment: <\/strong>If the disc in the temporomandibular joint is under slight displacement, splints may be used. In more severe cases, however, a surgical procedure known as <strong>arthrocentesis <\/strong>may be required.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#8211; <strong>Trigger point injections: <\/strong>A highly specialised and niche treatment performed only by the most qualified TMJ specialists in India. Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is among the few TMJ specialists in the country qualified to perform this intricate procedure.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With this general overview of TMJ conditions, symptoms, and treatment covered, let\u2019s go over the best TMJ specialists in India, where they currently serve, their expertise, and more.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Top 10 TMJ Specialists in India<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Right off the bat, it is important to note that while this is a list of the best TMJ specialists in the country, it is not a ranking list. As mentioned above, TMJ treatment is a highly specialised field in dentistry, and each of the specialists listed below is a medical veteran in 